        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "We are given the equation:\n\n\\[\n1 + A = \\frac{B}{C}\n\\]\n\nAnd the values:\n\n- \\( A' = 10.0584 \\)\n- \\( C = 0.510998950 \\)\n\nAssuming \\( A' \\) is the value of \\( A \\), we substitute into the equation:\n\n\\[\n1 + 10.0584 = \\frac{B}{0.510998950}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n11.0584 = \\frac{B}{0.510998950}\n\\]\n\nNow solve for \\( B \\):\n\n\\[\nB = 11.0584 \\times 0.510998950\n\\]\n\n\\[\nB \\approx 5.64783\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer:\n\\[\nB \\approx \\boxed{5.64783}\n\\]\n\nWould you like the result with more significant figures or in scientific notation?"
          ]
        },
